From 0d1b1b498e680f109514f19bda4b075a915000e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mphuongth <mphuongth@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 15:36:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(theme): unify app palette on navy + emerald
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The brand icon + PWA metadata already say navy/emerald (logo PR #127/#130,
rebrand PR #129), but the actual UI was still running on the old violet
system. This PR closes the gap so the whole app — landing, auth, PWA
splash, every nav, every form, every modal — speaks the same color
language as the logo.

## Color system

Light mode (`:root` in globals.css):
- --brand: #0F2A4A  (navy — wordmark, primary brand text)
- --brand-light: #ecfdf5  (emerald-50 — accent surface / hover bg)
- --brand-dark: #10B981  (emerald — active state / strong accent)

Dark mode (`.dark`):
- --brand: #F8FAFC  (cream — matches the icon peak stone)
- --brand-light: #0F2A4A  (navy — brand-tinted surface in dark mode)
- --brand-dark: #34D399  (mint — active state)

Role split:
- Navy is the *identity* color: wordmark, icon background, the "hero" card
  (portfolio value), PWA splash.
- Emerald is the *action* color: primary CTAs, active nav items, progress
  bars, link color, focus rings, growth indicators.
- Gains/losses stay green — emerald already ties the two together.

## What changed

Brand tokens:
- app/globals.css — flip all three --brand vars (light + dark)

Landing + auth + offline:
- app/page.tsx — bg gradient, signup CTA, hero gradient text, feature-card
  borders + icons, CTA section card, link colors
- app/auth/login/page.tsx, app/auth/signup/page.tsx — both pages refreshed:
  violet gradient "A" tile replaced with the Cairn icon; CTAs emerald;
  page bg same slate→emerald wash as the landing
- app/~offline/page.tsx — violet "A" tile → Cairn icon, button emerald

Chrome / nav:
- app/components/navigation/Sidebar.tsx — expanded + collapsed wordmark
  now uses `text-brand`; active nav item is emerald; profile avatar emerald

In-app components:
- app/assets/DashboardClient.tsx — goal-form submit button
- app/assets/components/NetWorthCard.tsx — chart stroke + gradient
  (#8b5cf6 → #10b981), empty-state accents
- app/assets/components/InsuranceCard.tsx — selected-card highlight,
  amount-saved text, focus ring, notice block, CTA
- app/assets/components/GoalPickerModal.tsx — selection highlight, hover,
  progress text, CTA
- app/assets/components/UnallocatedSection.tsx — hover text color; the
  `fund:` TYPE_BADGE entry unified with the purple used in the other
  ASSET_COLORS maps (categorical, not brand — purple stays distinct from
  emerald)
- app/(app)/settings/tabs/* (Savings, Fixed, Investments, Insurance
  Members) — cards, CTAs, totals panel, pagination
- app/(app)/planning/components/* (Insurance, FixedExpenses, Other,
  Savings, Funds, SalaryInput) — form CTAs, focus rings, loading spinner
- app/(app)/funds/FundLibraryClient.tsx — fund avatar chip, CTA

Shared primitives:
- components/ui/button.tsx — focus-visible ring + `link` variant color
- components/ui/input.tsx, select.tsx, textarea.tsx — focus border + ring

Screenshot generator (for the Android PWA install prompt):
- scripts/generate-screenshots.mjs — gradient bg, sidebar logo tile,
  active sidebar item, portfolio card label, progress bars. Navy stays
  on the "hero" card so it mirrors the actual app; progress fills are
  emerald (growth).
- public/screenshot-mobile.png, public/screenshot-desktop.png — regenerated

## What I didn't change

- ASSET_COLORS / TYPE_BADGE maps (fund: purple, bank: blue, gold: amber,
  stock: green) — those are categorical asset tags, not brand. Purple
  stays distinct from brand emerald.
- RELATIONSHIP_COLORS.Self — swapped to indigo so it's no longer the same
  hue as the old brand, but it's still a categorical tag.
- Chart palette #8b5cf6 in GoalCard / AssetAllocationPie — categorical
  colors for different asset slices; keeping distinct non-emerald hues
  for readability when many categories sit next to each other.

## Test plan

- [ ] Landing page: gradient bg is slate→emerald (not violet/pink), CTAs
  emerald, feature-card hover borders emerald, hero gradient text
  reads navy → emerald
- [ ] Auth pages (login, signup, email-sent): Cairn icon tile instead of
  purple "A"; CTAs emerald; bg matches landing
- [ ] Dashboard: sidebar collapsed shows "C" in brand navy (light) /
  cream (dark); expanded shows "Cairn" in brand; active nav item
  emerald-tinted
- [ ] Every form: focus ring on input / select / textarea is emerald
- [ ] Every primary CTA (`bg-emerald-600`) in modals and forms reads as
  the same color
- [ ] Net-worth chart line is emerald; empty-state divider emerald
- [ ] PWA install: splash stays navy; install screenshots preview the
  new emerald+navy UI

